        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "plain_text": " takes a Nordic lake landscape and redraws the whole thing as pattern: pink sky, dark mountain, a forest turned into folk motifs, water pooling in pale rings around a bridge. It's the most detailed piece in the gallery, worked stroke by stroke in coloured pencil, and it's the one print here that genuinely rewards the hundredth look. Which means hanging it where people sit rather than where they walk past. A reading corner, the wall beside a desk, anywhere you're close enough to keep finding things.",
