            "italic": false,
            "code": false,
            "strikethrough": false,
            "underline": false
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "plain_text": " is that wit in one image: an orange man with a Newton's cradle for eyes, one ball caught mid-swing, the face beneath it entirely deadpan. Physics happening on a forehead and nobody reacting. Wahlqvist draws with as few lines as he can get away with, and reckons a drawing's finished when it makes him laugh; this one clearly did. It's square, 50 x 50 cm, and it does more for a ",
          "href": null,
